---
title: Tiramisu
servings: 10
tags: [italian, vegetarian, make-ahead]
cuisine: italian
source: Tiramisù by GialloZafferano, https://www.giallozafferano.com/recipes/Tiramisu.html
---

Brew the @espresso{200%g}(moka pot coffee) and pour it into a wide, shallow
#bowl{} to cool.

Separate the @eggs{8}. Whisk the yolks with 100 g of the @sugar{200%g} in a
#stand mixer{} until pale and frothy. With the mixer running, add the
@mascarpone{1%kg} a little at a time until the cream is thick and firm.

With clean beaters, whisk the whites with the remaining 100 g of sugar to stiff
peaks.

Loosen the mascarpone cream with a spoonful of the whites, then gently fold in
the rest, lifting from the bottom.

Spread a generous layer of cream over the base of a 35 x 25 cm
#baking dish{}.

Dip the @ladyfingers{350%g}(about 42) quickly in the cold coffee, one side then
the other, and lay them in one direction for the first layer. Cover with about
half the remaining cream.

Make a second layer of dipped ladyfingers, cover with the rest of the cream and
smooth the top.

Dust with @cocoa powder{}(unsweetened) and refrigerate ~{2%hours} before
serving.

> The eggs are raw. Eat it the same day, or within 24 hours from the fridge;
> pasteurized eggs keep it 2 to 3 days.
